From aedb2a23013693ecb9d682d810be1fb6e0ec43d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:36:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Align claim screening and board shares with aged
 admission order

Follow-up to #3191 (t_a3dd31b927bb0457). The dispatcher now ranks ready and
review together by the aged admission score; two consumers that promise "the
dispatcher's own order" did not:

1. kanban_hub_admission_claim._candidates walked the ready lane, then appended
   review. A review card the claim pass reaches first could be deferred while
   lower-ranked ready cards spent the 3-call judge budget and were claimed.
   It now ranks the frozen ready+review lanes with
   order_with_remote_waiters (review only when review dispatch is on).

2. kanban_board_share.candidates ordered by raw SQL DISPATCH_ORDER with LIMIT
   and Candidate.rank compared priority only, so cross-board quotas ignored
   readiness aging (only the 2 h STARVE_SECONDS guard helped). Every eligible
   card is now scored with kanban_admission_score.rank before the cut, with
   one shared tick timestamp. Across boards a card's age counts from the later
   of its ready/review entry and its board's latest worker start, so a head
   the claim loop keeps skipping cannot age into every tick's first pick.
   STARVE_SECONDS stays as an independent per-board minimum-service guard.
   An unreadable score falls back to raw priority (dispatcher's fallback).

Tests: 4-card judge-budget review-first case + review-dispatch-off control;
cross-board aged-below-LIMIT winner, served-board age floor, score fallback.
